<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of</p>
<p>more than 10 million yen in the week to August 21 as released</p>
<p>by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.35 (0.35)	 one year     0.54 (0.57)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.91 (0.96)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.45 (0.46)	 three years  1.46 (1.50)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.31 (0.31)	 one year     0.49 (0.52)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.31 (0.31)	 two years    0.86 (0.91)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.41 (0.41)	 three years  1.41 (1.45)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.26 (0.26)	 one year     0.45 (0.48)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.27 (0.27)	 two years    0.81 (0.86)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.36 (0.36)	 three years  1.36 (1.40)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Aug 19 - Aug 23:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.50 (0.50)   120-150 days  0.50 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.52 (0.53)   150-180 days  UNQ  (UNQ )</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.60 (0.63)   180-360 days  0.70 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.62 (0.65)   over 360 days 1.00 (UNQ )</p>
</text>
